# Third-party content

## Agent personas — agents/

The nine agent persona files in `agents/` are vendored from the **agency-agents**
project by msitarzewski and contributors:

    https://github.com/msitarzewski/agency-agents

They are used under the MIT License (Copyright (c) 2025 AgentLand Contributors),
which permits redistribution. The upstream project states: "Use freely,
commercially or personally. Attribution appreciated but not required."

They are vendored rather than referenced so that an upstream change cannot alter
a persona in the middle of a pipeline run. Files are unmodified; see each file's
own frontmatter for its original name and description.

## Skills — referenced, not redistributed

The playbook invokes skills by name. None of their content is copied into this
repository; each comes from a plugin you install yourself, from the marketplace
named below.

| Skills | Plugin | Marketplace source |
|---|---|---|
| `code:instruction-generation`, `code:signatures`, `code:spec`, `code:spec-answered-questions`, `code:spec-check`, `code:spec-implement` | `code` | `bitovi/ai-enablement-prompts` (Bitovi, MIT) |
| `implement-workflow:ready-to-push` | `implement-workflow` | `bitovi/ai-enablement-prompts` (plugin authored by Mike Gvozdev) |
| `engineering:architecture`, `engineering:testing-strategy`, `engineering:code-review`, `engineering:documentation` | `engineering` | `anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins` (Anthropic) |
| `pskoett-ai-skills:simplify-and-harden`, `pskoett-ai-skills:self-improvement` | `pskoett-ai-skills` | `pskoett/pskoett-skills` (Peter Skøtt Pedersen, MIT) |

Install commands are in `README.md` § "Installing the skills the playbook names".

Unlike `agents/`, these are referenced rather than vendored: they are plugins with
their own update and versioning story, and two of the four are not ours to
redistribute. The trade-off is the one vendoring avoids — an upstream change can
alter a skill mid-run — so pin or vendor them yourself if a run must be reproducible.

The stages also run *without* these plugins installed: every stage prompt in the
playbook is a complete spec on its own, and instructs the agent to say so and follow
the prompt's structure when a named skill is not registered.
